Notebook[{
Cell["Penrose Graphical Calculus as Data: \:00a72.1.1\:20132.1.2", "Title"],
Cell["After Turaev & Virelizier, Monoidal Categories and Topological Field Theory, Ch. 2, pp. 31\:201333", "Subtitle"],
Cell["Start in a fresh kernel. Earlier notebooks in this series define f, g, m, n, id, vec and others as matrices or numbers, and leftover values can break the code below.", "Text"],
Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];", "Input"],
Cell["0. The symbols", "Section"],
Cell["f : X \:2192 Y: a morphism, drawn as a box. Diagrams are read bottom to top: lines below a box are its source, lines above are its target.", "Item"],
Cell["id_X: identity, drawn as a bare line coloured X. gf (= g\:2218f): first f, then g, drawn by stacking g above f.", "Item"],
Cell["\:2297: monoidal (tensor) product, drawn by juxtaposition. \|01d7d9: the unit object. A box with no lines below has source \|01d7d9; with none above, target \|01d7d9.", "Item"],
Cell["\:03c9 : X\:2297Y \:2192 \|01d7d9: a pairing, with inverse \:03a9 : \|01d7d9 \:2192 Y\:2297X. \:2228X: left dual. ev_X : \:2228X\:2297X \:2192 \|01d7d9 and coev_X : \|01d7d9 \:2192 X\:2297\:2228X. \:2228f : \:2228Y \:2192 \:2228X: the left dual of f.", "Item"],
Cell["1. The representation", "Section"],
Cell["A diagram is a list of boxes and a list of lines. A box carries its symbol inside it. A line is vertical. Its lower end either touches the top edge of a box (TopEdge) or is loose (Loose[y]). Its upper end either touches the bottom edge of a box (BottomEdge) or is loose.", "Text"],
Cell["MBox[name, symbol, {x1, x2}, y]: a box called name, showing symbol, spanning x1\:2026x2, centred at height y.", "Item"],
Cell["Strand[colour, x, lower, upper]: a line at horizontal position x, coloured by an object. lower is TopEdge[name] or Loose[y]; upper is BottomEdge[name] or Loose[y]. An optional 5th argument \"L\" puts the colour label on the left.", "Item"],
Cell["StringDiagram[{boxes\:2026}, {strands\:2026}]: the whole diagram.", "Item"],
Cell["(* ===== Representation and helpers ===== *)\nhgt = 0.5;                                        (* height of every box *)\nunit = \"\\|01d7d9\";                                 (* the unit object \|01d7d9 *)\nboxOf[StringDiagram[bs_, _], n_] := SelectFirst[bs, First[#] === n &];\nendY[d_, Loose[y_]] := y;                          (* height of a line end *)\nendY[d_, TopEdge[n_]] := boxOf[d, n][[4]] + hgt/2;\nendY[d_, BottomEdge[n_]] := boxOf[d, n][[4]] - hgt/2;\n\n(* how symbols and colours are typeset *)\ndispSym[s_String] := Which[\n   StringStartsQ[s, \"\\[Or]\"], Row[{Style[\"\\[Or]\", Smaller, Plain], Style[StringDrop[s, 1], Italic]}],\n   StringStartsQ[s, \"\\[CapitalOmega]\"] || s === unit, Style[s, Plain],\n   True, Style[s, Italic]];\ndispSym[Subscript[a_, b_]] := Subscript[Style[a, Plain], dispSym[b]];\ndispSym[e_] := e;\npretty[e_] := e /. {Subscript[a_String, b_] :> dispSym[Subscript[a, b]], s_String :> dispSym[s]};", "Input"],
Cell["(* ===== Renderer: StringDiagram -> picture ===== *)\nlabelY[w_, y1_, y2_] := Which[MatchQ[w[[3]], _Loose], y1 + 0.2, MatchQ[w[[4]], _Loose], y2 - 0.2, True, (y1 + y2)/2];\nrender[d : StringDiagram[bs_, ws_]] := Module[{lines, boxes, pts, xr, yr},\n   lines = Table[With[{x = w[[2]], y1 = endY[d, w[[3]]], y2 = endY[d, w[[4]]], left = Length[w] > 4},\n      {Black, AbsoluteThickness[2.4], Line[{{x, y1}, {x, y2}}],\n       Text[Style[dispSym[w[[1]]], 12, FontFamily -> \"Times\"],\n        {x + If[left, -0.08, 0.08], labelY[w, y1, y2]}, {If[left, 1, -1], 0}]}], {w, ws}];\n   boxes = Table[{EdgeForm[{Black, AbsoluteThickness[1.2]}], White,\n      Rectangle[{b[[3, 1]], b[[4]] - hgt/2}, {b[[3, 2]], b[[4]] + hgt/2}], Black,\n      Text[Style[dispSym[b[[2]]], If[Head[b[[2]]] === Subscript, 13, 15], FontFamily -> \"Times\"],\n       {Mean[b[[3]]], b[[4]]}]}, {b, bs}];\n   pts = Join[Flatten[Table[{{w[[2]], endY[d, w[[3]]]}, {w[[2]], endY[d, w[[4]]]}}, {w, ws}], 1],\n     Flatten[Table[{{b[[3, 1]], b[[4]] - hgt/2}, {b[[3, 2]], b[[4]] + hgt/2}}, {b, bs}], 1]];\n   {xr, yr} = CoordinateBounds[pts];\n   yr = {Min[yr[[1]], -1], Max[yr[[2]], 1]};\n   Graphics[{lines, boxes}, PlotRange -> {xr + {-0.45, 0.45}, yr + {-0.1, 0.1}},\n    ImageSize -> 62 (xr[[2]] - xr[[1]] + 0.9), BaselinePosition -> Axis]];", "Input"],
Cell["2. The transformation: diagram \:2192 expression", "Section"],
Cell["toExpression cuts the diagram into horizontal slices, one for each height at which a box sits. Inside a slice, everything is read left to right: each box gives its symbol, and each line passing through gives id of its colour. These are joined with \:2297 (CircleTimes). The slices are then composed from bottom to top with \:2218 (SmallCircle). Lines coloured \|01d7d9 are erased, as the book allows.", "Text"],
Cell["id[c_] := Subscript[\"id\", c];\ntensor[{}] := unit; tensor[{a_}] := a; tensor[l_List] := CircleTimes @@ l;\ncompose[{a_}] := a; compose[l_List] := SmallCircle @@ l;\n\ntoExpression[d : StringDiagram[bs_, ws0_]] := Module[{ws, levels, slice},\n   ws = Select[ws0, First[#] =!= unit &];\n   If[bs === {}, Return[tensor[id /@ First /@ SortBy[ws, #[[2]] &]]]];\n   levels = Union[#[[4]] & /@ bs];                     (* heights carrying boxes, bottom to top *)\n   slice[y_] := tensor[Last /@ SortBy[Join[\n        {#[[3, 1]], #[[2]]} & /@ Select[bs, #[[4]] == y &],                       (* boxes at this height *)\n        {#[[2]], id[#[[1]]]} & /@ Select[ws, endY[d, #[[3]]] < y < endY[d, #[[4]]] &]],  (* lines passing *)\n       First]];\n   compose[Reverse[slice /@ levels]]];\n\n(* types read off the picture: loose lower ends = source, loose upper ends = target *)\nobjs[l_] := tensor[First /@ SortBy[l, #[[2]] &]];\nsource[d_] := objs[Select[d[[2]], MatchQ[#[[3]], _Loose] &]];\ntarget[d_] := objs[Select[d[[2]], MatchQ[#[[4]], _Loose] &]];\nboxType[d_, n_] := objs[Select[d[[2]], #[[4]] === BottomEdge[n] &]] -> objs[Select[d[[2]], #[[3]] === TopEdge[n] &]];\n\nshow[d_] := Grid[{{render[d], Style[pretty[toExpression[d]], 17, FontFamily -> \"Times\"],\n     Style[Row[{pretty[source[d]], \"  \\[RightArrow]  \", pretty[target[d]]}], 12, GrayLevel[0.4]]}},\n   Spacings -> 3, Alignment -> {Left, Center}];\nshowEq[ds_List] := Column[{Row[Riffle[render /@ ds, Style[\"  =  \", 20, FontFamily -> \"Times\"]]],\n    Style[Row[Riffle[pretty[toExpression[#]] & /@ ds, \"   =   \"]], 16, FontFamily -> \"Times\"]}, Spacings -> 1];\n(* a one-box diagram on a single line *)\nmono[n_, s_, {x_, y_}, src_, tgt_, {bot_, top_}] :=\n  {MBox[n, s, {x - 0.28, x + 0.28}, y], {Strand[src, x, Loose[bot], BottomEdge[n]], Strand[tgt, x, TopEdge[n], Loose[top]]}};\njoin[parts__] := StringDiagram[Join @@ (Flatten[{#[[1]]}] & /@ {parts}), Join @@ (#[[2]] & /@ {parts})];", "Input"],
Cell["3. \:00a72.1.1: id_X, f and gf", "Section"],
Cell["idX = StringDiagram[{}, {Strand[\"X\", 0, Loose[-1], Loose[1]]}];\nfD = join[mono[\"f\", \"f\", {0, 0}, \"X\", \"Y\", {-1, 1}]];\ngfD = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"f\", \"f\", {-0.28, 0.28}, -0.9], MBox[\"g\", \"g\", {-0.28, 0.28}, 0.9]},\n   {Strand[\"X\", 0, Loose[-1.8], BottomEdge[\"f\"]], Strand[\"Y\", 0, TopEdge[\"f\"], BottomEdge[\"g\"]],\n    Strand[\"Z\", 0, TopEdge[\"g\"], Loose[1.8]]}];\nColumn[show /@ {idX, fD, gfD}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input"],
Cell["Here is what the data looks like, for gf:", "Text"],
Cell["gfD // InputForm", "Input"],
Cell["4. \:00a72.1.2: f \:2297 g", "Section"],
Cell["fgD = join[mono[\"f\", \"f\", {0, 0}, \"X\", \"Y\", {-1, 1}], mono[\"g\", \"g\", {1, 0}, \"U\", \"V\", {-1, 1}]];\nshow[fgD]", "Input"],
Cell["5. f : X\:2297Y \:2192 A\:2297B\:2297C, three ways", "Section"],
Cell["F[ws_] := StringDiagram[{MBox[\"F\", \"f\", {-0.3, 1.5}, 0]}, ws];\nf3a = F[{Strand[\"A\", 0, TopEdge[\"F\"], Loose[1]], Strand[\"B\", 0.6, TopEdge[\"F\"], Loose[1]],\n    Strand[\"C\", 1.2, TopEdge[\"F\"], Loose[1]],\n    Strand[\"X\", 0.3, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"F\"]], Strand[\"Y\", 0.9, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"F\"]]}];\nf3b = F[{Strand[\"A\", 0, TopEdge[\"F\"], Loose[1]], Strand[\"B\\[CircleTimes]C\", 1, TopEdge[\"F\"], Loose[1]],\n    Strand[\"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\", 0.4, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"F\"]]}];\nf3c = F[{Strand[\"A\\[CircleTimes]B\", 0.3, TopEdge[\"F\"], Loose[1], \"L\"], Strand[\"C\", 1.2, TopEdge[\"F\"], Loose[1]],\n    Strand[\"X\", 0.3, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"F\"]], Strand[\"Y\", 0.9, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"F\"]]}];\nColumn[show /@ {f3a, f3b, f3c}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input"],
Cell["6. \:03b1 : \|01d7d9 \:2192 \|01d7d9, \:03b2 : \|01d7d9 \:2192 X, \:03b3 : X \:2192 \|01d7d9", "Section"],
Cell["alD = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"a\", \"\\[Alpha]\", {-0.35, 0.35}, 0]}, {}];\nbeD = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"b\", \"\\[Beta]\", {-0.35, 0.35}, 0]}, {Strand[\"X\", 0, TopEdge[\"b\"], Loose[1]]}];\ngaD = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"c\", \"\\[Gamma]\", {-0.35, 0.35}, 0]}, {Strand[\"X\", 0, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"c\"]]}];\nColumn[show /@ {alD, beD, gaD}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input"],
Cell["7. Figure 2.1: The level-exchange property", "Section"],
Cell["ex[yf_, yg_] := join[mono[\"f\", \"f\", {0, yf}, \"X\", \"Y\", {-1.3, 1.3}], mono[\"g\", \"g\", {1, yg}, \"U\", \"V\", {-1.3, 1.3}]];\nfig21 = {ex[0, 0], ex[-0.55, 0.55], ex[0.55, -0.55]};\nshowEq[fig21]", "Input"],
Cell["The translation gives exactly the book's formula f\:2297g = (id_Y\:2297g)(f\:2297id_U) = (f\:2297id_V)(id_X\:2297g).", "Text"],
Cell["8. (2.1): A pairing \:03c9 and its inverse \:03a9", "Section"],
Cell["p1L = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"Om\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {-0.3, 0.7}, 0], MBox[\"om\", \"\\[Omega]\", {0.3, 1.3}, 0.9]},\n   {Strand[\"Y\", -0.1, TopEdge[\"Om\"], Loose[1.5], \"L\"], Strand[\"X\", 0.5, TopEdge[\"Om\"], BottomEdge[\"om\"]],\n    Strand[\"Y\", 1.1, Loose[-0.7], BottomEdge[\"om\"]]}];\nidY = StringDiagram[{}, {Strand[\"Y\", 0, Loose[-0.7], Loose[1.5]]}];\np1R = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"om\", \"\\[Omega]\", {-0.3, 0.7}, 0.9], MBox[\"Om\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {0.3, 1.3}, 0]},\n   {Strand[\"X\", -0.1, Loose[-0.7], BottomEdge[\"om\"], \"L\"], Strand[\"Y\", 0.5, TopEdge[\"Om\"], BottomEdge[\"om\"]],\n    Strand[\"X\", 1.1, TopEdge[\"Om\"], Loose[1.5]]}];\nidXb = StringDiagram[{}, {Strand[\"X\", 0, Loose[-0.7], Loose[1.5]]}];\nColumn[{showEq[{p1L, idY}], showEq[{p1R, idXb}]}, Spacings -> 3]", "Input"],
Cell["(* the types of the boxes, read off the diagram *)\n{boxType[p1L, \"Om\"], boxType[p1L, \"om\"]} // pretty", "Input"],
Cell["9. Uniqueness of the inverse", "Section"],
Cell["pairD[n_, s_, y_] := {MBox[n, s, {-0.3, 0.7}, y], {Strand[\"Y\", -0.1, TopEdge[n], Loose[1.4], \"L\"]}};\nu1 = join[pairD[\"Op\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]'\", -1], {{}, {Strand[\"X\", 0.5, TopEdge[\"Op\"], Loose[1.4]]}}];\nu2 = join[pairD[\"Op\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]'\", -1],\n   {{MBox[\"om\", \"\\[Omega]\", {0.3, 1.3}, 0.85], MBox[\"Om\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {0.9, 1.9}, 0]},\n    {Strand[\"X\", 0.5, TopEdge[\"Op\"], BottomEdge[\"om\"]], Strand[\"Y\", 1.1, TopEdge[\"Om\"], BottomEdge[\"om\"]],\n     Strand[\"X\", 1.7, TopEdge[\"Om\"], Loose[1.4]]}}];\nu3 = join[pairD[\"Op\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]'\", 0],\n   {{MBox[\"om\", \"\\[Omega]\", {0.3, 1.3}, 0.85], MBox[\"Om\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {0.9, 1.9}, -1]},\n    {Strand[\"X\", 0.5, TopEdge[\"Op\"], BottomEdge[\"om\"]], Strand[\"Y\", 1.1, TopEdge[\"Om\"], BottomEdge[\"om\"]],\n     Strand[\"X\", 1.7, TopEdge[\"Om\"], Loose[1.4]]}}];\nu4 = join[pairD[\"Om\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]\", -1], {{}, {Strand[\"X\", 0.5, TopEdge[\"Om\"], Loose[1.4]]}}];\nuniq = {u1, u2, u3, u4};\nshowEq[uniq]", "Input"],
Cell["10. The bijection (1.10) and its inverse", "Section"],
Cell["bijA = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"om\", \"\\[Omega]\", {-0.2, 0.8}, 0.9], MBox[\"a\", \"\\[Alpha]\", {0.4, 1.4}, 0]},\n   {Strand[\"X\", 0, Loose[-0.9], BottomEdge[\"om\"], \"L\"], Strand[\"Y\", 0.6, TopEdge[\"a\"], BottomEdge[\"om\"]],\n    Strand[\"T\", 1.2, TopEdge[\"a\"], Loose[1.5]], Strand[\"Z\", 0.9, Loose[-0.9], BottomEdge[\"a\"]]}];\nbijB = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"Om\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {-0.2, 0.8}, 0], MBox[\"b\", \"\\[Beta]\", {0.4, 1.4}, 0.9]},\n   {Strand[\"Y\", 0, TopEdge[\"Om\"], Loose[1.5], \"L\"], Strand[\"X\", 0.6, TopEdge[\"Om\"], BottomEdge[\"b\"]],\n    Strand[\"Z\", 1.2, Loose[-0.9], BottomEdge[\"b\"]], Strand[\"T\", 0.9, TopEdge[\"b\"], Loose[1.5]]}];\nColumn[{Row[{Style[\"\\[Alpha] \\[RightTeeArrow]  \", 18], show[bijA]}], Row[{Style[\"\\[Beta] \\[RightTeeArrow]  \", 18], show[bijB]}]}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input"],
Cell["11. The left dual \:2228f", "Section"],
Cell["dfL = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"df\", \"\\[Or]f\", {-0.3, 0.3}, 0]},\n   {Strand[\"\\[Or]Y\", 0, Loose[-1.6], BottomEdge[\"df\"], \"L\"], Strand[\"\\[Or]X\", 0, TopEdge[\"df\"], Loose[1.6], \"L\"]}];\ndfR = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"ev\", Subscript[\"ev\", \"Y\"], {-0.2, 0.9}, 1.1], MBox[\"f\", \"f\", {0.4, 0.9}, 0],\n    MBox[\"co\", Subscript[\"coev\", \"X\"], {0.4, 1.6}, -1.1]},\n   {Strand[\"\\[Or]Y\", 0, Loose[-1.6], BottomEdge[\"ev\"], \"L\"], Strand[\"Y\", 0.65, TopEdge[\"f\"], BottomEdge[\"ev\"]],\n    Strand[\"X\", 0.65, TopEdge[\"co\"], BottomEdge[\"f\"]], Strand[\"\\[Or]X\", 1.4, TopEdge[\"co\"], Loose[1.6]]}];\nshowEq[{dfL, dfR}]", "Input"],
Cell["12. (2.2)", "Section"],
Cell["e1 = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"ev\", Subscript[\"ev\", \"X\"], {-0.25, 0.9}, 1], MBox[\"df\", \"\\[Or]f\", {-0.25, 0.25}, 0]},\n   {Strand[\"\\[Or]X\", 0, TopEdge[\"df\"], BottomEdge[\"ev\"], \"L\"], Strand[\"\\[Or]Y\", 0, Loose[-0.9], BottomEdge[\"df\"], \"L\"],\n    Strand[\"X\", 0.7, Loose[-0.9], BottomEdge[\"ev\"]]}];\ne2 = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"ev\", Subscript[\"ev\", \"Y\"], {-0.25, 0.9}, 1], MBox[\"f\", \"f\", {0.45, 0.95}, 0]},\n   {Strand[\"\\[Or]Y\", 0, Loose[-0.9], BottomEdge[\"ev\"], \"L\"], Strand[\"Y\", 0.7, TopEdge[\"f\"], BottomEdge[\"ev\"]],\n    Strand[\"X\", 0.7, Loose[-0.9], BottomEdge[\"f\"]]}];\nc1 = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"co\", Subscript[\"coev\", \"Y\"], {-0.25, 0.95}, -1], MBox[\"df\", \"\\[Or]f\", {0.45, 0.95}, 0]},\n   {Strand[\"Y\", 0, TopEdge[\"co\"], Loose[0.9], \"L\"], Strand[\"\\[Or]Y\", 0.7, TopEdge[\"co\"], BottomEdge[\"df\"]],\n    Strand[\"\\[Or]X\", 0.7, TopEdge[\"df\"], Loose[0.9]]}];\nc2 = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"co\", Subscript[\"coev\", \"X\"], {-0.25, 0.95}, -1], MBox[\"f\", \"f\", {-0.25, 0.25}, 0]},\n   {Strand[\"X\", 0, TopEdge[\"co\"], BottomEdge[\"f\"], \"L\"], Strand[\"Y\", 0, TopEdge[\"f\"], Loose[0.9], \"L\"],\n    Strand[\"\\[Or]X\", 0.7, TopEdge[\"co\"], Loose[0.9]]}];\nColumn[{showEq[{e1, e2}], showEq[{c1, c2}]}, Spacings -> 3]", "Input"],
Cell["13. Evaluating the expressions in vector spaces", "Section"],
Cell["toMatrix interprets an expression in finite-dimensional vector spaces. Each colour gets a dimension, each box symbol gets a matrix, id_X becomes IdentityMatrix, \:2297 becomes KroneckerProduct and \:2218 becomes Dot. Every equation drawn above should then become an equality of matrices.", "Text"],
Cell["toMatrix[e_, dims_, mats_] := e /. Subscript[\"id\", c_] :> IdentityMatrix[dims[c]] /. Normal[mats] /.\n    {CircleTimes -> KroneckerProduct, SmallCircle -> Dot};\nvec[n_] := Flatten[IdentityMatrix[n]];\nfM = RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {3, 2}]; gM = RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}];\ndimsA = <|\"X\" -> 2, \"Y\" -> 3, \"U\" -> 2, \"V\" -> 2, \"\\[Or]X\" -> 2, \"\\[Or]Y\" -> 3|>;\nmatsA = <|\"f\" -> fM, \"g\" -> gM, \"\\[Or]f\" -> Transpose[fM],\n   Subscript[\"ev\", \"X\"] -> {vec[2]}, Subscript[\"ev\", \"Y\"] -> {vec[3]},\n   Subscript[\"coev\", \"X\"] -> Transpose[{vec[2]}], Subscript[\"coev\", \"Y\"] -> Transpose[{vec[3]}]|>;\nM = {{2, 1}, {1, 1}};                               (* \:03c9(x\:2297y) = x\:1d40 M y, a non-degenerate pairing on k\:00b2 *)\ndimsB = <|\"X\" -> 2, \"Y\" -> 2|>;\nmatsB = <|\"\\[Omega]\" -> {Flatten[M]}, \"\\[CapitalOmega]\" -> Transpose[{Flatten[Transpose[Inverse[M]]]}],\n   \"\\[CapitalOmega]'\" -> Transpose[{Flatten[Transpose[Inverse[M]]]}]|>;\nholds[ds_, dims_, mats_] := Equal @@ (toMatrix[toExpression[#], dims, mats] & /@ ds);\n<|\"Figure 2.1\" -> holds[fig21, dimsA, matsA],\n  \"(2.1) left\" -> holds[{p1L, idY}, dimsB, matsB], \"(2.1) right\" -> holds[{p1R, idXb}, dimsB, matsB],\n  \"uniqueness of \:03a9\" -> holds[uniq, dimsB, matsB],\n  \"definition of \:2228f\" -> holds[{dfL, dfR}, dimsA, matsA],\n  \"(2.2) ev\" -> holds[{e1, e2}, dimsA, matsA], \"(2.2) coev\" -> holds[{c1, c2}, dimsA, matsA]|>", "Input"],
Cell["14. Rewrite rules read off pp. 31\:201333", "Section"],
Cell["simplify[d] rewrites a diagram into another diagram. Every rule below comes from an equation in the pictures or from a convention stated in the text. Lines through a box are never moved, so each rewrite is a planar move.", "Text"],
Cell["Level exchange (Figure 2.1 and the text on functoriality of \:2297): boxes that do not touch can slide past each other vertically. This is used to bring two boxes next to each other, and to put a diagram in a normal form in which left boxes come first.", "Item"],
Cell["Unit strands (text after the \:03b1, \:03b2, \:03b3 pictures): a line coloured \|01d7d9 may be deleted.", "Item"],
Cell["\:2297-coloured lines (the three drawings of f : X\:2297Y \:2192 A\:2297B\:2297C): a line coloured A\:2297B is the same as two parallel lines A and B, with associativity ignored as in \:00a71.4.5.", "Item"],
Cell["(2.1) left and right zigzags: an inverse \:03a9 directly below its pairing \:03c9, joined by one line, straightens to an identity line. This applies to every pair (\:03c9, \:03a9), (\:03c9, \:03a9\:2032) and (ev_X, coev_X); coev_X is the inverse of the pairing ev_X.", "Item"],
Cell["Definition of \:2228f: the composite (ev_Y \:2297 id)(id \:2297 f \:2297 id)(id \:2297 coev_X) folds into a single box \:2228f.", "Item"],
Cell["(2.2): \:2228f slides through a cap or a cup and becomes f on the other leg: ev_X(\:2228f \:2297 id_X) \:2192 ev_Y(id_\:2228Y \:2297 f) and (id_Y \:2297 \:2228f)coev_Y \:2192 (f \:2297 id_\:2228X)coev_X.", "Item"],
Cell["Every rule removes boxes or removes \:2228's, so simplify always stops.", "Text"],
Cell["15. The layered form", "Section"],
Cell["LD[src, layers] lists the colours entering at the bottom, then one layer per box from bottom to top. A layer is {a, B[symbol, ins, outs]}, where a is the number of lines to the left of the box. toLayered and fromLayered convert between this form and StringDiagram. fromLayered places the lines and boxes automatically.", "Text"],
Cell["ins[B[_, i_, _]] := i; outs[B[_, _, o_]] := o; sym[B[s_, _, _]] := s;\nstepRow[row_, {a_, b_B}] := Join[Take[row, a], outs[b], Drop[row, a + Length[ins[b]]]];\nrows[LD[src_, ls_]] := FoldList[stepRow, src, ls];\nvalidQ[ld : LD[_, ls_]] := Quiet[Check[TrueQ[And @@ MapThread[\n      IntegerQ[#2[[1]]] && 0 <= #2[[1]] && #2[[1]] + Length[ins[#2[[2]]]] <= Length[#1] &&\n       Take[#1, {#2[[1]] + 1, #2[[1]] + Length[ins[#2[[2]]]]}] === ins[#2[[2]]] &, {Most[rows[ld]], ls}]], False]];\nvalidQ[_] := False;\nfromLayered::invalid = \"Layered diagram `1` is inconsistent: some box asks for lines that are not in its row.\";\n\n(* StringDiagram -> LD: sweep the boxes from bottom to top, left to right *)\ntoLayered[ld_LD] := ld;\ntoLayered[d : StringDiagram[bs_, ws_]] := Module[{idx = Range[Length[ws]], xOf, row, layers = {}, inW, outW, a},\n   xOf[i_] := ws[[i, 2]];\n   row = SortBy[Select[idx, MatchQ[ws[[#, 3]], _Loose] &], xOf];\n   Do[\n    inW = SortBy[Select[idx, ws[[#, 4]] === BottomEdge[b[[1]]] &], xOf];\n    outW = SortBy[Select[idx, ws[[#, 3]] === TopEdge[b[[1]]] &], xOf];\n    a = If[inW === {}, Count[row, i_ /; xOf[i] < Mean[b[[3]]]], First[FirstPosition[row, First[inW]]] - 1];\n    AppendTo[layers, {a, B[b[[2]], ws[[inW, 1]], ws[[outW, 1]]]}];\n    row = Join[Take[row, a], outW, Drop[row, a + Length[inW]]],\n    {b, SortBy[bs, {#[[4]], #[[3, 1]]} &]}];\n   LD[ws[[SortBy[Select[idx, MatchQ[ws[[#, 3]], _Loose] &], xOf], 1]], layers]];\n\n(* LD -> StringDiagram: columns by longest path in the left-to-right order, rows by dependency *)\nfromLayered[StringDiagram[a___]] := StringDiagram[a];\nfromLayered[ld : LD[src_, ls_]] /; validQ[ld] := Module[{cnt = 0, col = <||>, lower = <||>, upper = <||>, newW, row, rowsW, toks = {},\n    edges, preds, xi = <||>, nb = Length[ls], ports, sp, rk = <||>, ys, ymin, ymax, w0},\n   newW[c_, lo_] := (cnt++; col[cnt] = c; lower[cnt] = lo; cnt);\n   row = newW[#, \"src\"] & /@ src; rowsW = {row};\n   Do[With[{a = ls[[k, 1]], b = ls[[k, 2]]},\n      Module[{inW = Take[row, {a + 1, a + Length[ins[b]]}], outW},\n       Scan[(upper[#] = k) &, inW];\n       If[ins[b] === {} && outs[b] === {}, AppendTo[toks, Join[Take[row, a], {tok[k]}, Drop[row, a]]]];\n       outW = newW[#, k] & /@ outs[b];\n       row = Join[Take[row, a], outW, Drop[row, a + Length[inW]]];\n       AppendTo[rowsW, row]]], {k, nb}];\n   edges = Union @@ (Partition[#, 2, 1] & /@ Join[rowsW, toks]);\n   preds = GroupBy[edges, Last -> First];\n   Do[xi[v] = Max[0, 1 + (xi /@ Lookup[preds, Key[v], {}])],\n    {v, TopologicalSort[Graph[Join[Range[cnt], Cases[Flatten[toks], _tok]], DirectedEdge @@@ edges]]}];\n   ports[k_] := Select[Range[cnt], lower[#] === k || Lookup[upper, #, 0] === k &];\n   Do[With[{xs = If[ports[k] === {}, {0.8 xi[tok[k]]}, 0.8 (xi /@ ports[k])], s = sym[ls[[k, 2]]]},\n      w0 = Which[Head[s] === Subscript, 0.5, StringQ[s] && StringLength[s] > 1, 0.32, True, 0.28];\n      sp[k] = Mean[MinMax[xs]] + {-1, 1} Max[(Max[xs] - Min[xs])/2 + If[ports[k] === {}, 0.35, 0.28], w0]], {k, nb}];\n   Do[rk[k] = Max[0, 1 + (rk /@ Select[Range[k - 1], Function[j,\n          MemberQ[lower /@ Select[Range[cnt], Lookup[upper, #, 0] === k &], j] ||\n           (sp[j][[1]] < sp[k][[2]] + 0.05 && sp[k][[1]] < sp[j][[2]] + 0.05)]])], {k, nb}];\n   ys = Table[1.0 rk[k], {k, nb}];\n   {ymin, ymax} = If[nb == 0, {-0.2, 0.2}, MinMax[ys]];\n   StringDiagram[\n    Table[MBox[\"b\" <> ToString[k], sym[ls[[k, 2]]], sp[k], ys[[k]]], {k, nb}],\n    Table[Strand[col[w], 0.8 xi[w],\n      If[lower[w] === \"src\", Loose[ymin - 0.8], TopEdge[\"b\" <> ToString[lower[w]]]],\n      If[KeyExistsQ[upper, w], BottomEdge[\"b\" <> ToString[upper[w]]], Loose[ymax + 0.8]]], {w, cnt}]]];\nfromLayered[ld_LD] := (Message[fromLayered::invalid, Short[ld]]; $Failed);", "Input"],
Cell["(* Level exchange (Figure 2.1): swap two adjacent layers whose boxes do not touch *)\nswap[ls_, k_] := Module[{a = ls[[k, 1]], b1 = ls[[k, 2]], b = ls[[k + 1, 1]], b2 = ls[[k + 1, 2]], ni1, no1, ni2, no2, new},\n   {ni1, no1, ni2, no2} = Length /@ {ins[b1], outs[b1], ins[b2], outs[b2]};\n   new = Which[\n     b + ni2 <= a && ! (b == a && ni1 + no1 + ni2 + no2 == 0), {{b, b2}, {a - ni2 + no2, b1}},  (* upper box is to the left *)\n     b >= a + no1, {{b - no1 + ni1, b2}, {a, b1}},                                          (* upper box is to the right *)\n     True, $Failed];\n   If[new === $Failed, $Failed, Join[Take[ls, k - 1], new, Drop[ls, k + 1]]]];\n(* normal form: whenever an upper box is independent and to the left, let it drop below *)\nleftQ[ls_, k_] := With[{a = ls[[k, 1]], b1 = ls[[k, 2]], b = ls[[k + 1, 1]], b2 = ls[[k + 1, 2]]},\n   b + Length[ins[b2]] <= a && ! (b == a && Length[outs[b1]] == 0 && Length[ins[b2]] == 0)];\nnormalize[LD[src_, ls_]] := LD[src, FixedPoint[Function[l,\n     With[{k = SelectFirst[Range[Length[l] - 1], leftQ[l, #] &]}, If[MissingQ[k], l, swap[l, k]]]], ls, 1000]];\n(* move layer `from` to position `to` by level exchanges *)\nbubble[ls_, from_, to_] := Module[{l = ls, k = from},\n   While[k > to && l =!= $Failed, l = swap[l, k - 1]; k--];\n   While[k < to && l =!= $Failed, l = swap[l, k]; k++]; l];\n(* bring layers i < j next to each other; returns {layers, p} with them at p, p+1 *)\nmakeAdjacent[ls_, i_, j_] := Catch[\n   If[j == i + 1, Throw[{ls, i}]];\n   Do[With[{down = bubble[ls, m, i], up = bubble[ls, m, j]},\n     If[down =!= $Failed, With[{r = makeAdjacent[down, i + 1, j]}, If[r =!= $Failed, Throw[r]]]];\n     If[up =!= $Failed, With[{r = makeAdjacent[up, i, j - 1]}, If[r =!= $Failed, Throw[r]]]]], {m, i + 1, j - 1}];\n   $Failed];", "Input"],
Cell["16. The rules as code", "Section"],
Cell["pairings = {{\"\\[Omega]\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]\"}, {\"\\[Omega]\", \"\\[CapitalOmega]'\"}};   (* {pairing, inverse} *)\npairQ[w_, o_] := MemberQ[pairings, {w, o}] || MatchQ[{w, o}, {Subscript[\"ev\", x_], Subscript[\"coev\", x_]}];\ndualQ[s_] := StringQ[s] && StringStartsQ[s, \"\\[Or]\"];\nundual[s_String] := StringDrop[s, 1];\n\n(* (2.1): \:03a9 directly below \:03c9, joined by one line *)\nsnakeL[{a_, B[o_, {}, {_, _}]}, {b_, B[w_, {_, _}, {}]}] /; pairQ[w, o] && b == a + 1 := {};\nsnakeL[__] := $Failed;\nsnakeR[{a_, B[o_, {}, {_, _}]}, {b_, B[w_, {_, _}, {}]}] /; pairQ[w, o] && b == a - 1 := {};\nsnakeR[__] := $Failed;\n(* (2.2): slide \:2228f through ev or coev *)\nslideEv[{a_, B[s_?dualQ, {dy_}, {dx_}]}, {b_, B[Subscript[\"ev\", x_], {dx_, x_}, {}]}] /; b == a :=\n  {{a + 1, B[undual[s], {x}, {undual[dy]}]}, {a, B[Subscript[\"ev\", undual[dy]], {dy, undual[dy]}, {}]}};\nslideEv[__] := $Failed;\nslideCoev[{a_, B[Subscript[\"coev\", y_], {}, {y_, dy_}]}, {b_, B[s_?dualQ, {dy_}, {dx_}]}] /; b == a + 1 :=\n  {{a, B[Subscript[\"coev\", undual[dx]], {}, {undual[dx], dx}]}, {a, B[undual[s], {undual[dx]}, {y}]}};\nslideCoev[__] := $Failed;\n(* definition of \:2228f, read right to left *)\nfoldDual[{a_, B[Subscript[\"coev\", x_], {}, {x_, dx_}]}, {a2_, B[f_String, {x_}, {y_}]},\n    {a3_, B[Subscript[\"ev\", y_], {dy_, y_}, {}]}] /; a2 == a && a3 == a - 1 := {{a - 1, B[\"\\[Or]\" <> f, {dy}, {dx}]}};\nfoldDual[__] := $Failed;\n(* colour rules: unit strands vanish, \:2297-coloured strands split *)\nunitMap[c_] := If[c === unit, {}, {c}];\nsplitMap[c_String] := StringSplit[c, \"\\[CircleTimes]\"]; splitMap[c_] := {c};\nrecolour[ld : LD[src_, ls_], m_] := With[{f = Flatten[m /@ #] &},\n   LD[f[src], MapThread[{Length[f[Take[#1, #2[[1]]]]], B[sym[#2[[2]]], f[ins[#2[[2]]]], f[outs[#2[[2]]]]]} &,\n     {Most[rows[ld]], ls}]]];\n\nrules = <|\n   \"unit strands\" -> {\"colour\", unitMap},\n   \"\\[CircleTimes]-coloured strands\" -> {\"colour\", splitMap},\n   \"(2.1) left zigzag\" -> {2, snakeL},\n   \"(2.1) right zigzag\" -> {2, snakeR},\n   \"definition of \\[Or]f\" -> {3, foldDual},\n   \"(2.2) slide through ev\" -> {2, slideEv},\n   \"(2.2) slide through coev\" -> {2, slideCoev}|>;", "Input"],
Cell["17. simplify", "Section"],
Cell["try2[LD[src_, ls_], name_, r_] := Do[With[{adj = makeAdjacent[ls, i, j]},\n    If[adj =!= $Failed, With[{l = adj[[1]], p = adj[[2]]}, With[{rep = r[l[[p]], l[[p + 1]]]},\n       If[rep =!= $Failed, Throw[{name, LD[src, Join[Take[l, p - 1], rep, Drop[l, p + 1]]]}]]]]]],\n   {i, Length[ls] - 1}, {j, i + 1, Length[ls]}];\ntry3[LD[src_, ls_], name_, r_] := Do[With[{rep = r @@ ls[[k ;; k + 2]]},\n    If[rep =!= $Failed, Throw[{name, LD[src, Join[Take[ls, k - 1], rep, Drop[ls, k + 2]]]}]]], {k, Length[ls] - 2}];\nrewriteOnce[ld_LD, rs_Association] := Catch[\n   KeyValueMap[Function[{name, spec}, Switch[spec[[1]],\n      \"colour\", With[{new = recolour[ld, spec[[2]]]}, If[new =!= ld, Throw[{name, new}]]],\n      2, try2[ld, name, spec[[2]]],\n      3, try3[ld, name, spec[[2]]]]], rs];\n   $Failed];\n\n(* the list of {rule used, diagram} from start to finish *)\nsimplifyTrace[d_, rs_Association: rules] := Module[{ld = normalize[toLayered[d]], steps, r},\n   steps = {{\"start\", ld}};\n   While[(r = rewriteOnce[ld, rs]) =!= $Failed && Length[steps] < 50,\n    ld = normalize[r[[2]]]; AppendTo[steps, {r[[1]], ld}]];\n   steps];\nsimplifyLD[d_, rs_Association: rules] := Last[simplifyTrace[d, rs]][[2]];\nsimplify[d_, rs_Association: rules] := fromLayered[simplifyLD[d, rs]];   (* diagram -> diagram *)\nsameQ[d1_, d2_, rs_Association: rules] := simplifyLD[d1, rs] === simplifyLD[d2, rs];\n\nshowTrace[steps_] := Column[{\n    Row[Flatten[{render[fromLayered[steps[[1, 2]]]], Table[{\n         Column[{Style[steps[[k, 1]], 9, GrayLevel[0.35]], Style[\"\\[LongRightArrow]\", 22]}, Alignment -> Center],\n         render[fromLayered[steps[[k, 2]]]]}, {k, 2, Length[steps]}]}], \"  \"],\n    Style[Row[Riffle[pretty[toExpression[fromLayered[#[[2]]]]] & /@ steps, \"   \\[LongRightArrow]   \"]], 14, FontFamily -> \"Times\"]},\n   Spacings -> 1];", "Input"],
Cell["18. Tests on the examples of pp. 31\:201333", "Section"],
Cell["Figure 2.1: the three drawings have the same normal form, so level exchange alone identifies them.", "Text"],
Cell["nf = normalize[toLayered[#]] & /@ fig21;\n{Equal @@ nf, render[fromLayered[First[nf]]]}", "Input"],
Cell["(2.1): each zigzag straightens to a single line.", "Text"],
Cell["Column[{showTrace[simplifyTrace[p1L]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[p1R]]}, Spacings -> 3]", "Input"],
Cell["Uniqueness of the inverse. If the left zigzag is used first, the middle diagram simplifies to \:03a9. If the right zigzag is used first, it simplifies to \:03a9\:2032. Both are correct, so \:03a9\:2032 = \:03a9, which is the book's argument.", "Text"],
Cell["rulesRightFirst = Join[KeyTake[rules, {\"(2.1) right zigzag\"}], rules];\nColumn[{showTrace[simplifyTrace[u2]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[u2, rulesRightFirst]],\n   showTrace[simplifyTrace[u3]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[u3, rulesRightFirst]]}, Spacings -> 3]", "Input"],
Cell["The bijection (1.10): building the two maps with stackL (vertical) and besideL (\:2297), then simplifying, gives back the original box both ways round.", "Text"],
Cell["idL[cs_] := LD[cs, {}];\nboxL[s_, i_, o_] := LD[i, {{0, B[s, i, o]}}];\nstackL[l1 : LD[s1_, ls1_], LD[s2_, ls2_]] /; Last[rows[l1]] === s2 := LD[s1, Join[ls1, ls2]];   (* second on top *)\nbesideL[l1 : LD[s1_, ls1_], LD[s2_, ls2_]] := With[{n = Length[Last[rows[l1]]]},\n   LD[Join[s1, s2], Join[ls1, {#[[1]] + n, #[[2]]} & /@ ls2]]];\nforward[al_] := stackL[besideL[idL[{\"X\"}], al], besideL[boxL[\"\\[Omega]\", {\"X\", \"Y\"}, {}], idL[{\"T\"}]]];\nbackward[be_] := stackL[besideL[boxL[\"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {}, {\"Y\", \"X\"}], idL[{\"Z\"}]], besideL[idL[{\"Y\"}], be]];\nalL = boxL[\"\\[Alpha]\", {\"Z\"}, {\"Y\", \"T\"}]; beL = boxL[\"\\[Beta]\", {\"X\", \"Z\"}, {\"T\"}];\nColumn[{showTrace[simplifyTrace[backward[forward[alL]]]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[forward[backward[beL]]]]}, Spacings -> 3]", "Input"],
Cell["The definition of \:2228f, and (2.2):", "Text"],
Cell["Column[{showTrace[simplifyTrace[dfR]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[e1]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[c1]]}, Spacings -> 3]", "Input"],
Cell["Text conventions: strands coloured \|01d7d9 are erased, and the three drawings of f : X\:2297Y \:2192 A\:2297B\:2297C are the same morphism.", "Text"],
Cell["unitD = StringDiagram[{MBox[\"a\", \"\\[Alpha]\", {-0.35, 0.35}, 0], MBox[\"f\", \"f\", {0.8, 1.36}, 0]},\n   {Strand[unit, 0, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"a\"]], Strand[unit, 0, TopEdge[\"a\"], Loose[1]],\n    Strand[\"X\", 1.08, Loose[-1], BottomEdge[\"f\"]], Strand[\"Y\", 1.08, TopEdge[\"f\"], Loose[1]],\n    Strand[unit, 1.8, Loose[-1], Loose[1]]}];\nColumn[{showTrace[simplifyTrace[unitD]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[f3b]],\n   Equal @@ (simplifyLD /@ {f3a, f3b, f3c})}, Spacings -> 3]", "Input"],
Cell["19. Summary", "Section"],
Cell["Each rewrite step is also checked in vector spaces: the matrix of the diagram must not change.", "Text"],
Cell["dimsB2 = Join[dimsB, <|\"Z\" -> 2, \"T\" -> 2|>];\nmatsB2 = Join[matsB, <|\"\\[Alpha]\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {4, 2}], \"\\[Beta]\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 4}]|>];\nstepsKeep[steps_, dims_, mats_] := Equal @@ (toMatrix[toExpression[fromLayered[#[[2]]]], dims, mats] & /@ steps);\n<|\n \"Figure 2.1: one normal form\" -> Equal @@ nf,\n \"(2.1) left \\[Rule] id_Y\" -> sameQ[p1L, idY], \"(2.1) right \\[Rule] id_X\" -> sameQ[p1R, idXb],\n \"uniqueness: middle \\[Rule] \\[CapitalOmega]\" -> (simplifyLD[u2] === simplifyLD[u4] && simplifyLD[u3] === simplifyLD[u4]),\n \"uniqueness: middle \\[Rule] \\[CapitalOmega]'\" -> (simplifyLD[u2, rulesRightFirst] === simplifyLD[u1] && simplifyLD[u3, rulesRightFirst] === simplifyLD[u1]),\n \"bijection: backward\\[SmallCircle]forward = id\" -> (simplifyLD[backward[forward[alL]]] === alL),\n \"bijection: forward\\[SmallCircle]backward = id\" -> (simplifyLD[forward[backward[beL]]] === beL),\n \"definition of \\[Or]f\" -> sameQ[dfR, dfL], \"(2.2) ev\" -> sameQ[e1, e2], \"(2.2) coev\" -> sameQ[c1, c2],\n \"unit strands erased\" -> (simplifyLD[unitD] === LD[{\"X\"}, {{0, B[\"\\[Alpha]\", {}, {}]}, {0, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"Y\"}]}}] ||\n     simplifyLD[unitD] === normalize[LD[{\"X\"}, {{0, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"Y\"}]}, {1, B[\"\\[Alpha]\", {}, {}]}}]]),\n \"three drawings of f agree\" -> (Equal @@ (simplifyLD /@ {f3a, f3b, f3c})),\n \"every step keeps the matrix\" -> And @@ Join[\n    stepsKeep[simplifyTrace[#], dimsB2, matsB2] & /@ {p1L, p1R, u2, u3, backward[forward[alL]], forward[backward[beL]]},\n    {stepsKeep[simplifyTrace[u2, rulesRightFirst], dimsB2, matsB2]},\n    stepsKeep[simplifyTrace[#], dimsA, matsA] & /@ {dfR, e1, c1}],\n \"all layered forms valid\" -> And @@ (validQ[simplifyLD[#]] & /@ {p1L, u2, dfR, e1, c1, unitD, f3a})\n|>", "Input"],
Cell["\:00a9 Computational Classnotes \:00b7 CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "Text", TextAlignment -> Center, FontSlant -> "Italic"]
},
WindowTitle -> "Graphical calculus: data and simplify"]
